
LetsDefend SOC Environment

I used the LetsDefend SOC environment to gain hands-on experience working through simulated cybersecurity incidents in a Security Operations Center (SOC). The platform allowed me to analyze security alerts, investigate suspicious activity, review logs, and identify potential threats in a realistic SOC workflow.

Through these exercises, I practiced alert investigation, incident analysis, log analysis, threat detection, and incident response. I also worked with security events involving suspicious network activity, malware, authentication issues, and other common cybersecurity threats.

This experience helped me understand how security analysts monitor alerts, determine whether an event is a true or false positive, gather evidence, and document their findings. It also gave me practical experience applying cybersecurity concepts in a simulated enterprise environment.

Skills Demonstrated: SOC Operations • Alert Triage • Log Analysis • Incident Investigation • Threat Detection • Incident Response • Security Monitoring • Documentation
